SUMMARY:[Stanford Law] Interstate Intolerance
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261118T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261118T180000
DTSTAMP:20261113T202054Z
UID:stanford_campus-law-10003063-1795021200-1795024800@law.stanford.edu-20
 26-11-18T17:00:00-08:00@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Do we “want to live in a world where Texas is at war with Ca
 lifornia”? Justice Elena Kagan asked that question during oral argument 
 in a recent case. Increasingly the states seem to be answering yes. \nIn r
 ecent years\, states have banned official travel to states whose laws they
  dislike. They have sent tens of thousands of migrants to cities across th
 e country. They have made it a crime to seek certain medical care across s
 tate lines. Some have even sent National Guard troops into other states ov
 \n\nAges: All ages\nSource: https://law.stanford.edu/event/interstate-into
 lerance/\nLast synced: 2026-11-13 12:20 PST
LOCATION:@ SLS: Room 290\, 559 Nathan Abbott Way\, Stanford\, CA\, 94305-8
 610\, United States
URL:https://law.stanford.edu/event/interstate-intolerance/
END:VEVENT
